pan></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.33%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:9.5pt;">$</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:7.5%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:9.5pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_whfcl_SevenPointEightSevenFive2028NotesMember_P2XXXd7hbk2CQ-PxE9LXUw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LongTermDebtAverageAmountOutstanding" scale="3" id="Tc_J57BjoqwZEiolfFvKAwWDQ_8_11">190,205</ix:nonFraction></span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.33%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:9.5pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_AEfWhBXWI06wMjRnXNyedQ" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_JhbVsuegjkea5tPOoSHvUA" continuedAt="Tb_JhbVsuegjkea5tPOoSHvUA_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">NOTE&#160;7&#160;- RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Investment Advisory Agreement</span>: WhiteHorse Advisers serves as the Company&#8217;s investment adviser in accordance with the terms of an investment advisory agreement. <span style="color:#212529;">On November&#160;1, 2023, at an in-person meeting, the Company&#8217;s board of directors approved an amended and restated investment advisory agreement, which was executed by the Company on February 22, 2024 (the &#8220;Investment Advisory Agreement&#8221;). </span>The Company&#8217;s board of directors most recently re-approved the Investment Advisory Agreement on October 29, 2025. Subject to the overall supervision of the Company&#8217;s board of directors, WhiteHorse Advisers manages the day-to-day operations of, and provides investment management services to, the Company. Under the terms of the Investment Advisory Agreement, WhiteHorse Advisers:</p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">determines the composition of the investment portfolio, the nature and timing of the changes to the portfolio and the manner of implementing such changes;</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:12pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">identifies, evaluates and negotiates the structure of the investments the Company makes (including performing due diligence on the Company&#8217;s prospective portfolio companies); and</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">&#9679;</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">closes, monitors and administers the investments the Company makes, including the exercise of any voting or consent rights.</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In addition, WhiteHorse Advisers provides the Company with access to personnel and an Investment Committee. Under the Investment Advisory Agreement, the Company pays WhiteHorse Advisers a fee for investment management services consisting of a base management fee and an incentive fee. The Investment Advisory Agreement may be terminated by either party without penalty upon <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_boBTmCo9jUCCfF58NwrMEg" format="ixt-sec:durday" name="whfcl:InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementTerminationTerm" id="Narr_X-C8_1h-SUuaG-cjsoSscA">60</ix:nonNumeric>&#160;days&#8217; written notice to the other party.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Base Management Fee</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Effective January 1, 2024, the base management fee is calculated at an annual rate equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_1_1_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_ln5Vc8uvX0C1bfbuIg4Vsw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:PercentageOfBaseManagementFeeOnGrossAssets" scale="-2" id="Narr_mzYf-MAXjUaNVs-yaVZ30A">1.75</ix:nonFraction>% based on the Company&#8217;s consolidated gross assets (including cash and cash equivalents and assets purchased with borrowed funds); provided, however, the base management fee will be calculated at an annual rate equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_1_1_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_ln5Vc8uvX0C1bfbuIg4Vsw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:PercentageOfBaseManagementFeeOnGrossAssetsIfValueExceededTotalAssets" scale="-2" id="Narr_lpiIovQVqEiGKMH9aTQXmQ">1.25</ix:nonFraction>% of the Company&#8217;s consolidated gross assets (including cash and cash equivalents and assets purchased with borrowed funds), that exceed the product of (i)&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_1_1_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_ln5Vc8uvX0C1bfbuIg4Vsw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:ThresholdPercentageForCalculationOfBaseManagementFee" scale="-2" id="Narr_3kEY9qwH-E-F_yESDXAtNA">200</ix:nonFraction>% and (ii)&#160;the value of the Company&#8217;s total net assets, at the end of the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_QCjiDdjIfU6xHc3oczi4_Q" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_1_1_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_ln5Vc8uvX0C1bfbuIg4Vsw" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="whfcl:NumberOfCalendarQuarters" scale="0" id="Narr_Slo8_m4ooke5x1bX-5rbqw">two</ix:nonFraction> most recently completed calendar quarters. Base management fees are payable quarterly in arrears and are appropriately pro-rated for any partial&#160;month or quarter.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;">Prior to January 1, 2024, the base management fee is calculated at an annual rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_stXRyCqD1kuhwgxfdxFwHA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:PercentageOfBaseManagementFeeOnGrossAssets" scale="-2" id="Narr_Z6oyzN_ADUax_QOnS9jrYg">2.00</ix:nonFraction>% based on the Company&#8217;s consolidated gross assets (including cash and cash equivalents and assets purchased with borrowed funds); provided, however, the base management fee will be calculated at an annual rate equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_stXRyCqD1kuhwgxfdxFwHA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:PercentageOfBaseManagementFeeOnGrossAssetsIfValueExceededTotalAssets" scale="-2" id="Narr_6j-sPNKPJU61L7VjI47NSA">1.25</ix:nonFraction>% of the Company&#8217;s consolidated gross assets (including cash and cash equivalents and assets purchased with borrowed funds) that exceed the product of </p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:3pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:3pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">175</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">WHITEHORSE FINANCE,&#160;INC.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">Notes To Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">December&#160;31, 2025</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;">(in thousands, except share and per share data)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_-YM89MjF006e2AX462qZFw_1_3"></a><a id="Tc_Xj9ZeU0Pf0yH7AoHES59NA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_WG2zhm0UNEqgksGs02OAGw_2_3"></a><a id="Tc_-fvunRMDBkasjM8WGqX48g_2_6"></a><a id="Tc_vxTnYgBOE0CiXJ9wQAMbTA_2_9"></a><a id="Tc_2EruKOgIv0yrgM8s5M5MyQ_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_2kLWtymqDE-K77yCj0ntvA_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_j98CvL89HEaQP1fXIjeblA_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_mYY8f7dPq0WMn_SYfFh4QA_3_8"></a><a id="Tc_0CE0IBD3sE6hJVhzyPddEw_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_lrNoeNQ1ZkmFuLemIw6_ng_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_Z3INq_VEJ06s_E7GjyhakQ_4_5"></a><a id="Tc_bu3zm3P9Sk-AJlj39wZIew_4_8"></a><ix:continuation id="Tb_JhbVsuegjkea5tPOoSHvUA_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_JhbVsuegjkea5tPOoSHvUA_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(i)&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OB6QXf9I0kejVMhTvRVYrQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_stXRyCqD1kuhwgxfdxFwHA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:ThresholdPercentageForCalculationOfBaseManagementFee" scale="-2" id="Narr_PCf_W0tDWUuLKx4uShHRkQ">200</ix:nonFraction>% and (ii)&#160;the value of the Company&#8217;s total net assets, at the end of the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_QCjiDdjIfU6xHc3oczi4_Q" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementMember_stXRyCqD1kuhwgxfdxFwHA" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="whfcl:NumberOfCalendarQuarters" scale="0" id="Narr_7INksuYpnUyJVuhtwfIszQ">two</ix:nonFraction> most recently completed calendar quarters. Base management fees are payable quarterly in arrears and are appropriately pro-rated for any partial&#160;month or quarter.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The following table details our management fee expenses for the years ended December&#160;31, 2025, 2024 and 2023:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_AEfWhBXWI06wMjRnXNyedQ" name="whfcl:ScheduleOfManagementFeeExpensesTableTextBlock" id="Tb_KzmC_z_-h0WtV9yWen5Dvw" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;min-height:0.0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:0pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:47.08%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.77%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:12.77%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.04%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td></tr><tr style=""><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:47.08%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New R