023_nb1DxQMsuUelLkNFgYfiiQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:PerformanceBasedIncentiveFees" scale="3" id="Tc_PjxZX7_-3kujg173SROvaA_6_9">10,678</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31,&#160;2024, incentive fees payable on the consolidated statements of assets and liabilities were $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_SASgKsac4kuJ0Ja_NInCHg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:IncentiveFeePayables" scale="3" id="Narr_KaKl7ZzwvUeDH5NYPv1hLw">19,157</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_qm5B7k34nkWN9MUq-lwkuw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="whfcl:IncentiveFeePayables" scale="3" id="Narr_YAzVyhGwG02Y3HR_FtDYhQ">17,848</ix:nonFraction>, respectively.<span style="letter-spacing:0.2pt;"> </span>As of both December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31, 2024, there were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_CapitalGainsIncentiveFeesMember_mrFy8Oi2RUGo0YVWiPc-GA" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="whfcl:IncentiveFeePayables" scale="3" id="Narr_tiEiQ5xz2UaTJbfAtNReww"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_whfcl_CapitalGainsIncentiveFeesMember_taGNvbCTm0mDcpPCezoTFw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="whfcl:IncentiveFeePayables" scale="3" id="Narr_hpHKhKIEjki-pH2r2N5nOg">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> incentive fees payable on the consolidated statements of assets and liabilities for cumulative accruals of Capital Gains Incentive Fees under GAAP, including any amounts payable pursuant to the Investment Advisory Agreement as described above.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Administration Agreement</span>: Pursuant to the Administration Agreement, WhiteHorse Administration furnishes the Company with office facilities, equipment and clerical, bookkeeping and record keeping services to enable the Company to operate. Under the Administration Agreement, WhiteHorse Administration performs, or oversees the performance of, the Company&#8217;s required administrative services, which include being responsible for the financial records which the Company is required to maintain and preparing reports to its stockholders and reports filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. In addition, WhiteHorse Administration assists the Company in determining and publishing its net asset value, oversees the preparation and filing of its tax returns and the printing and dissemination of reports to its stockholders and generally oversees the payment of the Company&#8217;s expenses and the performance of administrative and professional services rendered to the Company by others. Payments under the Administration Agreement equal an amount based upon the Company&#8217;s allocable portion of WhiteHorse Administration&#8217;s overhead in performing its obligations under the Administration Agreement, including rent and the Company&#8217;s allocable portion of the cost of its chief financial officer and chief compliance officer along with their respective staffs. Under the Administration Agreement, WhiteHorse Administration also provides on the Company&#8217;s behalf managerial assistance to those portfolio companies to which the Company is required to provide such assistance. The Administration Agreement may be terminated by either party without penalty upon <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_KhmMMQAxzUCSKo7_qwI3cQ" format="ixt-sec:durday" name="whfcl:InvestmentAdvisoryAgreementTerminationTerm" id="Narr_Ofwj3uQh-0OZVAOkmuiNGg">60</ix:nonNumeric>&#160;days&#8217; written notice to the other party. To the extent that WhiteHorse Administration outsources any of its functions, the Company will pay the fees associated with such functions on a direct basis without any profit to WhiteHorse Administration.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:3pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:3pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">178</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:79.3%;border:0;margin:30pt 10.35% 30pt 10.35%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:10.35%;padding-right:10.35%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:41.75pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">WHITEHORSE FINANCE,&#160;INC.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">Notes To Consolidated Financial Statements</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">December&#160;31, 2025</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 6pt 0pt;">(in thousands, except share and per share data)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_JhbVsuegjkea5tPOoSHvUA_cont4"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Substantially all the Company&#8217;s payments of operating expenses to third parties were made by a related party, for which such third party received reimbursement from the Company.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During each of the years ended December&#160;31,&#160;2025, 2024 and 2023, the Company incurred allocated administrative service fees of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_doU3YE8SEUaZ9-jxscBPxg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdministrativeFeesExpense" scale="3" id="Narr_FllWysPPCkmYOI5l3_zTnQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_TqUQseEdT0qLUdHRWA-dvA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdministrativeFeesExpense" scale="3" id="Narr_8PeOcR4BEUS_gS_MWLTiSA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_KhmMMQAxzUCSKo7_qwI3cQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:AdministrativeFeesExpense" scale="3" id="Narr_4XWMmYFk406_KGo8ZAmbdg">683</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Co-investments with Related Parties</span>: As of December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31,&#160;2024, no officers or employees affiliated with or employed by WhiteHorse Advisers and its related entities maintained any co-investments in the Company&#8217;s investments.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31,&#160;2024, certain funds affiliated with WhiteHorse Advisers and its related entities maintained co-investments in the Company&#8217;s investments of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_WhiteHorseAdvisersMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_iHWbi4nbUk-0EgLLGcHc2A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilities" scale="3" id="Narr_w3u1NC9wMUy1UEVW9upMSw">7,220,543</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_WhiteHorseAdvisersMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_ZDcToRGGTku39h7MiHVrRQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilities" scale="3" id="Narr_ah_DjarI7kqIg-NIWlltpg">5,890,052</ix:nonFraction>, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">STRS JV</span>: For the year ended December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December 31, 2024, the Company sold $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_StrsJvMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_Z4Sm7hkHPEqwQeLgvH2ycw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForProceedsFromInvestments" scale="3" id="Narr_kjnT3w-hjUic9iKaPw-aSA">83,259</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_StrsJvMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_qrcgknCIdkCGRMUffqBFRA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:PaymentsForProceedsFromInvestments" scale="3" id="Narr_Vvh866oX7Eyon-pn6i-LHQ">59,190</ix:nonFraction> of investments to STRS JV and recognized a net realized loss of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_StrsJvMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_Z4Sm7hkHPEqwQeLgvH2ycw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RealizedInvestmentGainsLosses" sign="-" scale="3" id="Narr_-EhSB9rW50mbLJ3c6TRKlA">4</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_whfcl_StrsJvMember_us-gaap_TypeOfArrangementAxis_whfcl_AdministrationAgreementMember_qrcgknCIdkCGRMUffqBFRA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RealizedInvestmentGainsLosses" sign="-" scale="3" id="Narr_WtFYi7W0ekSPzpuwRtVW9w">15</ix:nonFraction>, respectively. </p></ix:continuation><a id="_14c34bbf_0044_4092_af62_85c57043c6ae"></a><a id="Tc_Pe_rGDG5Lk2T-qq-iFMAzg_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_I4_gzjuRzkuX__r5Uuy_BA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_a9p-siemLUOrVbjzoSRsxA_1_5"></a><a id="Tc_fB5fLj2GEkOAf59Tj94KOA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_VCwXMkXwhUujWyqRUd23YQ_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_L25qHME0EkSGl7_J5iI29A_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_IdjTQoyyN0KIXYm6Aky5mw_3_3"></a><a id="Tc_mMyUoo79002F5hYBg1YRVQ_3_5"></a><a id="Tc_e3sGLVnHa0iqqHO7Fxqo1A_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_Et_9JeZ52k6GV90V4gXyeQ_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_bacQNK5YfE2oY5bsMewACg_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_J5z3EcWtaUa4V-c8C5LL-g_6_3"></a><a id="Tc_b6KjDhlPX0CFiAi5ow_Kfw_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_h1Sdv1DRr0etIYusDA58qg_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_uGYcOgtGVkmtVOGOFNv7tg_8_6"></a><a id="Tc_ZNeqV-iG7EGm2rDfLUVQfQ_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_hGjrHOhK2kmA_-OiYv7P8Q_10_0"></a><a id="Tc_Lp-uG4VGZUKK_huzd5Xqmg_10_6"></a><a id="Tc_yFDhfnIJ7EC5PzT3JIfESg_11_0"></a><a id="Tc_XK_jg5F2ik6LNf5MTk8TyQ_11_6"></a><a id="Tc_0y8BMxj2kkeBCNyvtc-Ofw_12_0"></a><a id="Tc_nA-nD1k9Nk-_rEwBV_Ntdw_13_0"></a><a id="Tc_jvZna_MRjUC3n_kjIbdr4A_14_0"></a><a id="Tc_Lf-jgSZ9IEuIsqhKtY3I5g_14_6"></a><a id="Tc_CXgcdeytPUyMnqdC2_2ixA_15_0"></a><a id="Tc_NKm5vPU2z0Go8DX2JKkmfg_15_6"></a><a id="Tc_Uk-9B8ablUaufU__v1CiqA_16_0"></a><a id="Tc_6iBGqKmRPUyzFSzku4mPNg_16_3"></a><a id="Tc_Yek2NUEL006YlLo66iw5pg_17_0"></a><a id="Tc_MMe4BWQf20CdQ1CoK0IW0g_17_6"></a><a id="Tc_fcLWo216OUCxXpf2IySdDw_18_0"></a><a id="Tc_F9vuZRvRO0-oRdSNAlo1UQ_19_0"></a><a id="Tc_-7BeunbvcUm_ynt04Dla8w_20_0"></a><a id="Tc_JBKUAdAo-km_8VWgMMTCpw_20_6"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_AEfWhBXWI06wMjRnXNyedQ" name="us-gaap:CommitmentsAndContingenciesDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_KNiEiyWgskOm1ck-HkyWWw" continuedAt="Tb_KNiEiyWgskOm1ck-HkyWWw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">NOTE&#160;8&#160;- COMMITMENTS AND CONTINGENCIES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Commitments</span>: In the normal course of business, the Company is party to financial instruments with off-balance-sheet risk to meet the financing needs of its borrowers. These financial instruments include commitments to extend credit and involve, to varying degrees, elements of credit risk in excess of the amount recognized in the consolidated statement of assets and liabilities. The Company attempts to limit its credit risk by conducting extensive due diligence and obtaining collateral where appropriate.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31,&#160;2024, the balance of unfunded commitments to extend credit was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_SASgKsac4kuJ0Ja_NInCHg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:UnusedCommitmentsToExtendCredit" scale="3" id="Narr_7W9iqA1ZCEmHJW092rgBuw">40,994</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_FFkwHGwPOkyNVvvR70yQzA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_qm5B7k34nkWN9MUq-lwkuw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:UnusedCommitmentsToExtendCredit" scale="3" id="Narr_MWg-4zhYjEmPA661GT4_Cg">26,385</ix:nonFraction>, respectively. Commitments to extend credit consist principally of the unused portions of commitments that obligate the Company to extend credit, such as revolving credit arrangements or similar transactions. These commitments are often subject to financial or non-financial milestones and other conditions to borrow that must be achieved before the commitment can be drawn. In addition, the commitments generally have fixed expiration dates or other termination clauses. Since commitments may expire without being drawn upon, the total commitment amounts do not necessarily represent future cash requirements.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;">The following table summarizes the Company&#8217;s unfunded commitments as of December&#160;31,&#160;2025 and December&#160;31,&#160;2024:</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_AEfWhBXWI06wMjRnXNyedQ" name="us-gaap:OtherCommitmentsTableTextBlock" id="Tb_a7h-HEY6vkaj4nq1yPVo0A" continuedAt="Tb_a7h-HEY6vkaj4nq1yPVo0A_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:6pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;width:57.24%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="position:absolute;top:0pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></th><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></th><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.43%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></th><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:17.09%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></th><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.85%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></th><th style="font-weight:normal;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.43%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;positio